    "id": "train-5614",
    "question": "Jules is walking dogs to help pay for his family's vacation. The vacation costs $1,000. There are five members in his family and each one must contribute the same amount towards the vacation cost. He charges $2 to start a walk and $1.25 per block. If he walks 20 dogs, how many blocks in total does he have to walk them?",
    "gold": "128",
    "answer": "Jules has to earn $200 because 1000 / 5 = <<1000/5=200>>200\nHe has earned $40 from starting the walks because 20 x 2 = <<20*2=40>>40\nHe has to earn $160 from distance, because 200 - 40 = <<200-40=160>>160\nHe has to walk 128 blocks because 160 / 1.25 = <<160/1.25=128>>128\n#### 128"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many blocks Jules has to walk the dogs, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount Jules needs to contribute towards the vacation.\n2. Determine how much Jules earns from walking the dogs.\n3. Calculate the total number of blocks Jules needs to walk the dogs.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total amount Jules needs to contribute.**\n\nThe vacation costs $1,000 and there are five members in Jules's family. Therefore, each family member needs to contribute:\n\\[\n\\frac{1000}{5} = 200 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine how much Jules earns from walking the dogs.**\n\nJules charges $2 to start a walk and $1.25 per block. If he walks 20 dogs, the total number of blocks he walks is:\n\\[\n20 \\text{ dogs} \\times 20 \\text{ blocks per dog} = 400 \\text{ blocks}\n\\]\nThe total earnings from walking the dogs is:\n\\[\n20 \\text{ dogs} \\times 2 \\text{ dollars per dog} + 400 \\text{ blocks} \\times 1.25 \\text{ dollars per block} = 40 \\text{ dollars} + 500 \\text{ dollars} = 540 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total number of blocks Jules needs to walk the dogs.**\n\nSince Jules needs to earn $200 to contribute $200 towards the vacation, and he earns $540 from walking the dogs, the number of blocks he needs to walk is:\n\\[\n\\frac{540 \\text{ dollars}}{1.25 \\text{ dollars per block}} = 432 \\text{ blocks}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of blocks Jules has to walk the dogs is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{432}\n\\]",
